From: OpenMPTCProuter maintainers
Subject: mqvpn: backport Linux recovery and server stability fixes for v0.62.14

Backports selected from upstream mqvpn after ca1e4f3:
  5a7e1c9  fix(netlink): treat admin down as immediate path drop
  840f692  fix(netlink): gate path re-add on usable address of server family
  1feebf1  fix(netlink): exclude v4 link-local and require carrier in re-add gate
  b907484  fix(platform): drive engine after netlink-driven path changes
  220a2e6  fix(client): honor CREATE_WAIT retry deadline in tick interest
  0051cf7  fix(linux): drop path on RTM_DELADDR when no usable source remains
  0bcee8a  feat(api): add Linux platform path-drop reasons
  554a9c5  refactor(linux): share drop-by-interface handling
  be5941b  fix(linux): let link events own DELADDR races on down links

Also includes the Linux-only behavior from dbaae1b (drive/re-arm after
TUN-originated sends), the server pre-handshake context lifetime fix from
3cb574a, and the live primary path-id 0 abandon fix from a92e664.

xquic 540330f is intentionally not included: it fixes a leak introduced by
the later dynamic paths_info refactor. In xquic 9e588b6 paths_info is inline
storage, so that commit would free a non-heap object and fails compilation
with -Werror=free-nonheap-object.

The patch is intentionally based on mqvpn b23a4ae with xquic 9e588b6
after OpenMPTCProuter patches 001-004.

